From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek shorten board SerDes retry grace

The XR1710G board opts into the RTK flow_s recovery state machine.  After
the Airoha paired USXGMII replay, the first flow_s pulse can leave copper
link up while the in-band carrier remains down.  Waiting for the generic
120-second grace window delays recovery and blocks LAN DHCP.  Retry the
board-specific flow_s pulse after five PHY polls so the paired replay can
recover within seconds while preserving the existing state machine and
its carrier checks.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6-Astra
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
index 9f8cb9f..e6a0ad3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -26,5 +26,5 @@
 
 /* Let the HZ-driven PCS poll observe the new in-band word before retrying. */
-#define RTL826X_RTK_SERDES_CARRIER_GRACE_POLLS	120
+#define RTL826X_RTK_SERDES_CARRIER_GRACE_POLLS	5
 
 #define RTL8201F_IER				0x13
-- 
2.43.0
